<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><Bill type="bill" xmlns="http://leg.wa.gov/2012/document"><BillHeading><RequestNumber>H-0282.1</RequestNumber><ShortBillId>HB 1103</ShortBillId><LongBillId>HOUSE BILL 1103</LongBillId><Legislature>68th Legislature</Legislature><Session>2023 Regular Session</Session><Sponsors>Representatives Fey, Barkis, and Wylie</Sponsors><BillHistory><PrefiledDate>Prefiled 01/03/23.</PrefiledDate><ReadDate>Read first time 01/09/23.</ReadDate><ReferredCommittee>Referred to Committee on Transportation.</ReferredCommittee></BillHistory><BriefDescription>Avoiding interest arbitrage charges on bond proceeds in the capital vessel replacement account.</BriefDescription></BillHeading>

<BillBody>
<BillTitle>AN ACT Relating to avoiding interest arbitrage charges on bond proceeds in the capital vessel replacement account; amending 2022 c 186 s 406 (uncodified); and creating a new section.</BillTitle>
<EnactedClause />
<BillSection type="new" xmlns="http://leg.wa.gov/2012/document">
<BillSectionHeader><BillSectionNumber><TextRun>Sec. </TextRun><Value>1</Value><TextRun>.  </TextRun></BillSectionNumber><P>The legislature finds that delays in the procurement of additional ferry boat vessels have correspondingly delayed the time frame in which the proceeds of bonds issued for that purpose may be spent. The legislature further finds that, absent timely legislative action, the state may be subject to internal revenue service arbitrage rebate penalties for failure to expend the bond proceeds in a timely manner. It is the intent of the legislature to repurpose the bond proceeds to allow the department of transportation to spend the funds within internal revenue service timelines.</P></BillSectionHeader>
</BillSection>
